---
import { menuLinks, siteConfig } from "@/site.config";

const year = new Date().getFullYear();
---

{/*
	Each row stays on ONE line at every width, including a 390px phone. The type
	is text-xs everywhere (not just at sm:).

	The two rows no longer sit side by side, and that is what a SIXTH nav item
	cost. Measured in the browser at 1280px: the copyright line wants 347px and
	six links at px-3 want 416px, which with the 16px gap is 779px against the
	768px the column gives (--content-max caps at 48rem until the viewport
	passes ~1422px, and above that the root font grows with it, so the column
	never gets relatively roomier). Five links needed 697px and fitted; six do
	not, and no padding value rescues it -- at the 704px of content left at
	1024px even px-1.5 lands at 707px. So they stack, which costs one line of
	footer and removes the whole class of problem.

	The nav padding is still responsive, because stacking does not help the
	phone: six labels are 272px of text on their own, and only px-1.5 fits them
	into the 358px a 390px phone gives us.

	  390px   px-1.5   344px of 358px
	  640px   px-3     416px of 576px

	Do not restore flex-wrap. Wrapping was a previous fix for the nav
	overflowing the viewport; the real fix is fitting, and any change here must
	be re-checked for horizontal overflow at 390px, not just for line count.
*/}
<footer
	class="text-muted mt-auto flex w-full flex-col items-center justify-center gap-y-2 pt-20 pb-4 text-center align-top text-xs font-semibold"
>
	<div class="font-normal">
		{/* The space before <span> is written explicitly: Astro trims the newline
		    between a text node and a following element, which ran the two
		    sentences together as "Koonkor.Built on". */}
		&copy; {year} {siteConfig.author}.{" "}<span class="inline-block">
			Built on <a
				class="hover:text-global-text hover:underline"
				href="https://github.com/chrismwilliams/astro-theme-cactus"
				rel="noreferrer"
				target="_blank">Astro Cactus</a
			>.
		</span>
	</div>
	<nav aria-label="Footer" class="divide-muted flex justify-center divide-x">
		{
			menuLinks.map((link) => (
				<a class="hover:text-global-text px-1.5 py-1 hover:underline sm:px-3" href={link.path}>
					{link.title}
				</a>
			))
		}
	</nav>
</footer>
